// The state-visibility red line (wyrd-h5e): after binding r2 to an update of r,
// r STILL denotes the original. Every update yields a new value; no binding a
// program already holds can observe a later "change"
// (proposal-value-semantics-mvp §3.4). This is what makes the whole update
// surface value-semantics-honest, and it is checked operationally by the
// eval == run differential.
def r = #{ x = 1, y = 2 };

// Update THROUGH a new binding r2; r is not mentioned as a target.
def r2 = #{ r | x = 9 };

// Return the ORIGINAL r -- it is unchanged. r2 would render #{x=9, y=2}.
r

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: #{x = 1, y = 2}
